	<!--Unit preferences for production-->

	<!--Note: Base preferences should loosely match Defensive preferences. This is because defensive is usually unit spam
		and offensive is heavy unit spam. A base preference should match unit spam as some personalities have dedicated states
		for making heavy units when there is a balance of power to ensure there isnt any over representation of T3 in spam.-->
	
	<!--Engineers, Commandos, other Special Infantry/Vehicles as well as RELOAD_AIRCRAFT and BOMBER_AIRCRAFT count as
		context specific units and must be set to 0% here and created/managed via a state instead to prevent dormant 
		units sitting on airfield decks or having a faction only fight with them and lose stupendously-->
	
	<!--Offensive Preference: Takes into consideration the WeaponTemplate of a GameObject Asset but not all aspects of it
		Percentages should be assigned in coordinance with unit usability, context and general effectivenss (Micro, AOE)
		to compensate for the lack of aspects not considered (Ex: The SkirmishAI Unit Builder 'thinks' the shatterer
		is an extremely good unit because of its AOE and sonic dps but in reality it can be dodged, therefore offensive
		percentage assignment must take this into account to rebalance it for the Unit Builder Algorithm-->
	
	<!--Defensive Preference: Takes into consideration the Body (HP) and ArmorTemplate but not speed/agility
		Percentages should be assigned based on how durable but also how maneuverable the unit really is and for
		infantry, crushing must be taken into consideration strongly as well as the fact their effectiveness
		is primarily horde based at the Unit chooser level-->
	
	<!--Overall Offensive & Defensive Preferences may be used to scale or over emphasize the real effectiveness of
		units between each other. This could/might be used to scale down the Defensive Modifier for Infantry so that
		the AI doesnt make them in more proportions than is determined for any given battle scenario. Generally spam 
		Infantry when on heavy defense or far behind for a quick boost and cut them down from the main body of the army
		when things stabilize. High tier infantry can be made exceptions to this (Shock/Zone Troopers/BH inf)-->
	
	<!--On unit composition: UnitBuilder params also exist in personality templates, those are the default if they are 
		not defined here. Define it for Critical Defense spam so its cost effective while defending and doesnt spam 
		expensive T3 but keep it blank for base preference. Percentages otherwise
		largely do not matter but it might be worth contrasting between vehicles and infantry to avoid too much
		representation of infantry.-->
	
